<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="demo">
  <h2>Full inheritance vs. an explicit allowlist</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>Compare the two ways of launching the same local MCP server below — one hands over everything in the shell, one hands over exactly what the server declared it needs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>The broken version is the default you get from not specifying <code>env</code> at all, or explicitly passing <code>process.env</code> for convenience. The fixed version builds the <code>env</code> object from an explicit allowlist.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>Note the fixed version's allowlist is the same shape as the MCP TypeScript SDK's own <code>getDefaultEnvironment()</code> — this isn't a novel pattern, it's what the SDK already does when you don't override it.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="case-demo"
           aria-label="Spawning a local MCP server with full environment inheritance vs. an explicit allowlisted environment"
           data-required="true"
