{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A locally spawned MCP server gets your whole shell environment by default unless you explicitly limit it — including secrets that have nothing to do with what the server does.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Build the <code>env</code> passed to the spawn call as an explicit allowlist of exactly the variables that server needs, the same way the MCP SDK's own <code>getDefaultEnvironment()</code> does by default.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Scoping doesn't prevent a compromise, it caps the blast radius of one — a vulnerability in a scoped server can only leak what was actually in its environment, not everything that happened to be in the developer's shell that day.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
